  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3455",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3455: Important priority package update for kernel",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-98993:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnamespace: don't inherit MNT_UMOUNT in clone_mnt()\n\nCVE-2026-98863:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: x86: Re-pend GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES if getting said pages fails\n\nCVE-2026-98056:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme: remove stale namespaces by NSID range during scan\n\nCVE-2026-89912:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: vgic-its: Don't dereference a NULL collection on ITT save\n\nCVE-2026-72434:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: ipset: make sure gc is properly stopped\n\nCVE-2026-43456:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbonding: fix type confusion in bond_setup_by_slave()\n",
